#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:17
msgid ""
"Fix crash when `# fmt: skip` follows the closing bracket of a multi-line "
"call or subscript that isn't the last element of a collection or argument "
"list ([#5522](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5522))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:19
msgid ""
"Normalize hex codes in unicode escape sequences in f-strings ([#5526]"
"(https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5526))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:20
msgid ""
"Fix `--stdin` output ending in `\\r\\r\\n` instead of `\\r\\n` when the "
"input uses CRLF line endings and does not end with a newline, e.g. a "
"notebook piped to `black -` ([#5559](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5559))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:23
msgid ""
"Fix crash when `# fmt: skip` on an opening bracket is followed by more code "
"after the closing bracket, such as `x = [  # fmt: skip` ... `] + [3]` "
"([#5538](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5538))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:25
msgid ""
"Fix a parenthesized lambda being turned into a tuple when a standalone "
"comment sits in one of its parameter defaults ([#5533](https://github.com/"
"psf/black/pull/5533))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:27
msgid ""
"Fix crash when `# fmt: skip` follows the closing parenthesis of a multi-line "
"`from` import and another statement on the same line, such as `); import c  "
"# fmt: skip` ([#5584](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5584))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:30
msgid ""
"Fix `--skip-magic-trailing-comma` dropping the trailing comma from a split "
"one-element subscript (`a[x,]`) used as a lambda parameter default ([#5533]"
"(https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5533))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:32
msgid ""
"Fix crash on bytes literals containing `\\u`, `\\U` or `\\N{...}`, which are "
"not escape sequences in bytes and were changed by the escape normalization "
"([#5583](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5583))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:34
msgid ""
"Fix a parenthesized lambda being turned into a tuple when a standalone "
"comment sits between `lambda` and its parameters ([#5596](https://github.com/"
"psf/black/pull/5596))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:36
msgid ""
"Fix crash on `# fmt: skip` after a one-line compound statement whose "
"semicolon-separated body starts with a bare name, such as `if x: a; b` "
"([#5588](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5588))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:38
msgid ""
"Keep comments at the end of a `# fmt: off` region inside brackets unchanged, "
"instead of moving a trailing comment to its own line or re-indenting them "
"([#5585](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5585))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:40
msgid ""
"Fix crash when `# fmt: skip` is on an opening bracket and a conditional "
"expression continues after the closing bracket, such as `x = (  # fmt: "
"skip` ... `) if c else d` ([#5586](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5586))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:43
msgid ""
"Fix a compound statement header right after a comment-only `# fmt: off` / `# "
"fmt: on` block being merged into the `# fmt: on` comment when the header has "
"`# fmt: skip` or is outside the selected `--line-ranges` ([#5549](https://"
"github.com/psf/black/pull/5549))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:46
msgid ""
"Fix crash when a compound statement header with `# fmt: skip` contains a "
"bracket that has its own `# fmt: skip` on the opening line ([#5597](https://"
"github.com/psf/black/pull/5597), [#5612](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/"
"5612))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:48
msgid ""
"Fix unstable formatting of a call with an inline comment after an argument "
"when its last argument is an implicitly concatenated string ([#5587](https://"
"github.com/psf/black/pull/5587))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:50
msgid ""
"Keep the empty lines before a comment outside the requested `--line-ranges` "
"instead of capping them ([#5613](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5613))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:52
msgid ""
"Fix a `# fmt: skip` comment on a line of its own after a blank line skipping "
"the statement above it, which removed or added blank lines and could crash "
"with \"produced different code on the second pass\" ([#5615](https://"
"github.com/psf/black/pull/5615))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:55
msgid ""
"Fix crash on an assignment whose target is split over lines inside redundant "
"parentheses and doesn't fit on one line with the value, such as "
"`(a.b(c)` ... `.d[e]) = f` ([#5606](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5606), "
"[#5621](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5621))"
msgstr ""

