#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:145
msgid "Version 26.10.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:149
msgid ""
"This release fixes a security issue in Black's bundled GitHub Action. "
"Repositories that use the action are encouraged to update to the latest "
"version of Black immediately. This update is received automatically when "
"using `psf/black@stable`, and is independent of the version of Black "
"installed by the action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:154
msgid ""
"When the GitHub Action reads version specifiers from `tool.black.required-"
"version`, it now only accepts released versions of Black, as it already did "
"for `black` requirements in dependency lists. Other values, such as URL "
"references, are now rejected. This issue has been registered as `GHSA-cg8m-"
"r9f2-5wm2`; a CVE identifier is pending."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:161
msgid ""
"Fix a long Jupyter notebook assignment magic (for example `x = !ls -la`) "
"being wrapped in parentheses, which IPython can no longer run; such cells "
"are now left unchanged ([#5481](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5481))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:164
msgid ""
"Keep repeated lines outside the selected `--line-ranges` unchanged ([#5436]"
"(https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5436))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:165
msgid ""
"Fix `--line-ranges` formatting lines that follow a statement when formatting "
"joins or re-indents that statement ([#5484](https://github.com/psf/black/"
"pull/5484))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:167
msgid ""
"Fix `--line-ranges` crashing with an internal error when an unselected "
"statement has a `# fmt: skip` comment on the last line before a closing "
"bracket ([#5477](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5477))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:169
msgid ""
"Prevent moving an encoding declaration (for example `# -*- coding: latin-1 "
"-*-`) onto the first two lines of a file ([#5487](https://github.com/psf/"
"black/pull/5487))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:171
msgid ""
"Fix adding an extra trailing blank line inside a multi-line module docstring "
"when its last line is near the line length limit ([#5494](https://github.com/"
"psf/black/pull/5494))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:173
msgid ""
"Keep the parentheses around a walrus that is the only item in a set (for "
"example `{(x := f())}`) when targeting Python 3.9 or older, since Python 3.8 "
"and 3.9.0 can't parse it without them ([#5502](https://github.com/psf/black/"
"pull/5502))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:179
msgid ""
"Do not split short expressions on delimiters (such as binary operators, "
"comparisons, or comprehensions) inside brackets when preceded by a "
"standalone comment ([#5455](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5455))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:181
msgid ""
"Fix the unstable `string_processing` feature removing backslash-newline "
"sequences from raw strings, which changed their value ([#5482](https://"
"github.com/psf/black/pull/5482))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:183
msgid ""
"Avoid adding unnecessary parentheses around unbreakable right-hand side "
"expressions in assignments (such as annotated assignments or subscript "
"targets) ([#5473](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5473))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:185
msgid ""
"Parenthesize expressions with parameter comments when they exceed the line "
"length under `--preview` ([#5442](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5442))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:187
msgid ""
"Fix `wrap_long_dict_values_in_parens` dropping the parentheses around a "
"right-hand side that contains a dictionary, leaving a line over the length "
"limit ([#5492](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5492))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:189
msgid ""
"Fix the unstable `string_processing` feature adding a space after `*` or "
"`**` in a PEP 695 type parameter (`* Ts = ...`) when it splits a string in "
"the parameter's default ([#5504](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5504))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:192
msgid ""
"Avoid unnecessary line splits of trailers (such as indexing/subscripts) when "
"an earlier bracket split exceeds the line length only due to a trailing "
"comment ([#5498](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5498))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:197
msgid ""
"Add `--cache-dir` to configure the cache directory from the command line "
"([#5433](https://github.com/psf/black/pull/5433))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGES.md:198
msgid ""
"Don't cache a file as formatted after formatting or checking it with `--line-"
